ATP is a specification + docs repo (Markdown spec, README, examples, JSON Schemas, conformance shell scripts, Python check scripts) that also holds a Python package, the ATP client in clients/python (clients/python/pyproject.toml): pip builds it with setuptools when it installs it (run: pip install ./clients/python), and it is not published to a package index. The unit test suites are scripts/test_checks.py, the unit tests for the check scripts (run: python3 scripts/test_checks.py), and clients/python/tests/test_atp_client.py, the unit tests for the client (run: cd clients/python && pip install . && python -m unittest discover -s tests); the conformance test suite (conformance/level1.sh, conformance/level2.sh) tests a running authority. There is no lint configuration, so no lint step applies.
